# SoulSearch DwarfSpec Component Testing

## Objective

Create live DwarfSpec coverage for SoulSearch behavior that depends on the real
DFHack widget tree, renderer, focus system, pointer routing, complete-screen
lifecycle, or overlay lifecycle.

Keep pure search, filtering, sorting, formatting, persistence, and catalog
rules in the existing Busted suite. Component specs should verify visible
behavior and native interaction instead of duplicating those unit assertions.

## Phase 1 - Test Layout

- [x] Store ordinary component specs under `tests/components/`.
- [x] Name live tests `*.ds.lua` so default DwarfSpec discovery finds them.
- [x] Reserve `tests/components/support/` for reusable factories as ordinary
      `.lua` modules that are not discovered as specs.
- [x] Keep `tests/dwarfspec/config.lua` absent because the default recursive
      `*.ds.lua` discovery and default wait settings match this project.
- [x] Confirm `dwarfspec list` discovers every component spec without loading
      or executing it.

## Phase 2 - Shared Support

- [x] Add deterministic result, filter-choice, preset-choice, and stats-subject
      factories.
- [x] Use Busted spies for asserting rendered user interactions without
      replacing native widgets.
- [x] Add a live-unit helper that selects a valid unit without mutating it.
- [x] Add stable `view_id` values to the main screen's window and tooltip
      children so DwarfSpec can traverse them without `subject:raw()`.
- [x] Use `subject:raw()` only for native state that DwarfSpec does not expose.
- [x] Ensure every spec relies on DwarfSpec-owned cleanup and leaves no screen,
      overlay, pointer state, or persisted configuration behind.

## Phase 3 - Filter Action List

Target: `tests/components/filter_action_list.ds.lua`

- [x] Clicking each visible action zone dispatches the correct filter ID and action.
- [x] Disabled priority actions do not dispatch at list boundaries.
- [x] Hovering an action displays its dynamic tooltip.
- [x] Hovering a descriptor displays the descriptor tooltip.
- [x] Action hit-testing remains correct after scrolling.
- [x] Clicking outside a complete action row delegates without dispatching.

## Phase 4 - Modal Panels And Pickers

Target: `tests/components/pickers.ds.lua`

- [x] Opening a modal panel makes it visible and gives it focus.
- [x] Opening a searchable picker focuses its search field.
- [x] Typing in a picker invokes its query callback with the rendered text.
- [x] Submitting a picker item passes the correct descriptor.
- [x] Submitting a picker item leaves the picker open for repeated selection.
- [x] Right-clicking inside an open modal dismisses it after child input has priority.
- [x] The close button dismisses the picker and releases focus.
- [x] An open modal consumes pointer input that would otherwise reach controls underneath it.
- [x] Attribute rows display attribute descriptions when hovered.
- [x] Race rows display the race-filter tooltip when hovered.
- [x] Unit-scope rows display the candidate-scope tooltip when hovered.
- [x] Preset submission routes custom, default, and role choices correctly.
- [x] Saving a preset invokes the save callback while preserving entered search text.

## Phase 5 - Filter Panel

Target: `tests/components/filter_panel.ds.lua`

- [x] Opening the panel renders active filters and refreshes picker choices.
- [x] Attribute, skill, race, unit-scope, and preset buttons open the correct picker.
- [x] Opening one picker closes the currently open picker.
- [x] Closing the filter panel also closes its active picker.
- [x] Selecting a picker item updates the rendered active-filter list.
- [x] Direction controls update the rendered filter direction.
- [x] Priority controls move the rendered filter row in the expected direction.
- [x] Remove controls remove the rendered filter row.
- [x] Reset filters clears the list and updates the active-filter counter.
- [x] Keyboard shortcuts perform the same actions as corresponding buttons.
- [x] Picker content renders above and receives input before the list beneath it.

## Phase 6 - Results Panel

Target: `tests/components/results_panel.ds.lua`

- [x] Typing in Search invokes `on_query` and preserves the displayed text.
- [x] Clicking a result changes selection and invokes `on_select` with that result.
- [x] Up and Down move the result cursor without requiring an initial click.
- [x] Submitting a row invokes `on_submit` with the selected result.
- [x] Replacing choices preserves the requested selected row.
- [x] Clicking each column header dispatches its declared sort column.
- [x] Repeated header clicks visibly cycle ascending, descending, and unsorted indicators.
- [x] Changing sort indicators does not disturb result selection.
- [x] Hovering each column header displays its declared tooltip.
- [x] Resizing preserves header alignment, list geometry, and scrolling.

## Phase 7 - Unit Information

Target: `tests/components/unit_info_panel.ds.lua`

- [x] A subject renders its unit name and title.
- [x] A subject renders its matched-filter heading and criteria.
- [x] A subject renders its meaningful stat records.
- [x] Replacing the subject refreshes identity, matched filters, and stats.
- [x] Clearing the subject clears all subject-dependent content.
- [x] Matched-filter content changes its section height without overlap.
- [x] Clicking Stat cycles stat-name ordering and its visible indicator.
- [x] Clicking Delta cycles value ordering and its visible indicator.
- [x] Stat sort state remains independent from result sorting.
- [x] Hovering a stat label displays its attribute description.
- [x] Hovering a delta value displays the baseline-difference tooltip.
- [x] A constrained viewport renders a usable scrollbar and aligned columns.
- [x] Adaptive columns account for a visible scrollbar.
- [x] Resizing reflows identity, matched filters, and stats without clipping.
- [x] Resetting view state restores the requested sort and first visible row.

## Phase 8 - Complete SoulSearch Screen

Target: `tests/components/main_screen.ds.lua`

- [x] The complete screen mounts through `ds.mount()` and completes a real render.
- [x] Search initially owns focus and the result list accepts navigation input.
- [x] Typing a query changes the visible result set.
- [x] Selecting another result refreshes the unit information panel.
- [x] Opening the filter panel gives its modal controls input priority.
- [x] Adding or removing a filter recomputes visible rankings.
- [x] Loading a preset refreshes filters, candidates, results, and stats once.
- [x] Result sorting and stat sorting operate independently.
- [x] Hovering buttons, headers, filter actions, and stats displays the correct tooltip.
- [x] A modal picker's tooltip takes precedence over controls underneath it.
- [x] Dragging and resizing retain stable geometry during the mount.
- [x] Closing the screen persists eligible frame changes once.
- [x] Dismissal unregisters the screen and restores normal input ownership.
- [x] Cleanup remains idempotent when dismissal and destruction both occur.

## Stats Overlay Component

Target: `tests/components/stats_overlay.ds.lua`

- [x] The isolated overlay receives its normal enable, update, input, render, and disable lifecycle.
- [x] A valid live unit renders identity and stats.
- [x] Changing the live unit refreshes the rendered subject.
- [x] Losing the unit-card subject hides or clears stale unit content.
- [x] Collapse hides the panel while retaining its deployment control.
- [x] Expand restores the panel at its prior position.
- [x] Collapse and expand arrows point in the correct direction for docking.
- [x] Alternate viewport sizes preserve docking and usable panel geometry.
- [x] Stat sorting works through the mounted column control.
- [x] Header and body tooltips render above the clipped popout.
- [x] Unmount disables and removes the overlay without retaining UI state.

## Creatures Overlay Component

Target: `tests/components/creatures_overlay.ds.lua`

- [x] The isolated overlay mounts through `ds.mount()` and completes a real render.
- [x] The launch button is visible for the Residents tab.
- [x] The launch button is visible for the Pets/Livestock tab.
- [x] The launch button is visible for the supported Other-unit tab.
- [x] Unsupported tabs keep the overlay hidden and do not initialize a search.
- [x] Clicking the launch button opens SoulSearch with the correct candidate scope.
- [x] Repeated layout updates keep the button docked below the native tab.
- [x] Unmount disables and removes the overlay cleanly.

## Overlay Registration Integration

Keep these specs separate from ordinary component discovery and select them
explicitly because they exercise external DFHack registration and persisted
overlay state.

Target: `tests/integration/overlay_registration.integration.lua`

- [x] Stage the stats overlay script with `ds.stage_overlay_registration()`.
- [x] Stage the Creatures overlay script with `ds.stage_overlay_registration()`.
- [x] Verify `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` discovery and rescan registration.
- [x] Verify enablement and disablement through the real overlay framework.
- [x] Verify focus filtering against the supported native screens.
- [x] Verify configured positioning is applied by the real overlay framework.
- [x] Verify cleanup restores `overlay.json` byte for byte.
- [x] Verify cleanup removes only unchanged, run-owned staged scripts.
- [x] Verify a final rescan leaves no staged registration behind.

## Explicit Exclusions

- [ ] Do not duplicate pure search scoring and ranking assertions.
- [ ] Do not duplicate filter catalog, preset, or role mapping assertions.
- [ ] Do not duplicate sort-state transition-table assertions.
- [ ] Do not duplicate presenter string-formatting assertions.
- [ ] Do not mutate fortress units merely to prepare component fixtures.
- [ ] Do not use isolated overlay mounts to claim real registration coverage.
- [ ] Do not treat mocked Busted widget tests as live DwarfSpec evidence.

## Verification

- [ ] `dwarfspec list` reports every ordinary component spec.
- [x] `dwarfspec run` passes the complete ordinary component suite.
- [x] Each explicitly selected overlay-registration integration spec passes.
- [ ] `busted` continues to pass the native unit suite.
- [ ] The Lua build and syntax validation continues to pass.
- [ ] A deliberately failing component example still cleans up its mounted UI.
- [ ] No run leaves screens, overlays, staged scripts, or modified configuration behind.
- [ ] Record DFHack version, DwarfSpec version, viewport, command, result, and date.

